---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Privacy"
  description="How this website handles enquiry details, local message preparation and links to WhatsApp and email."
>
  <article class="section container prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Website information</p>
    <h1>Your privacy.</h1>
    <p>
      This website is operated for Polished & Pristine Mobile, based in Darlington. For questions
      about your information, email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Preparing an enquiry</h2>
    <p>
      The quote builder prepares a message in your browser. It does not send your details to a
      website server or save them in browser storage. When you choose to open WhatsApp or email,
      your message is passed to that service so you can review and send it. Those services process
      information under their own privacy policies.
    </p>
    <h2>When you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Information you choose to send, such as your name, vehicle, location and photographs, is used
      to respond to your enquiry, discuss a quote and arrange the requested service. Contact us if
      you want to ask about, correct or request deletion of information you have shared. Some
      information may need to be retained to meet legal obligations.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not set analytics or advertising cookies. It does not embed social media
      trackers, external fonts or third-party videos. The hosting provider may process standard
      technical information, such as IP addresses and request logs, to deliver and secure the
      website.
    </p>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      The Areas We Cover page offers an optional Google map. No Google Maps embed is requested until
      you select “Load Google map”. Loading it connects your browser to Google, which receives
      technical information such as your IP address and may use cookies under its own policies. You
      can hide the map again or use the external map link instead. See{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google’s privacy information<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      WhatsApp, telephone and email links open services outside this website. Check the relevant
      provider’s privacy information when using them.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
